---
// The card-stack island's server shell.
//
// The active location is passed as SLOT CONTENT, never as a prop (issue #121).
// Astro serialises every island prop into the `props` attribute of
// `<astro-island>`, so rendering the card to a string here shipped the whole
// thing TWICE — once as real DOM, once JSON-escaped, the nested islands' own
// props (all 268 browse cards) included. Measured at 757 KB of 1.53 MB on a
// filtered lens page.
//
// Slot content is emitted as real DOM inside `<astro-slot>` and never enters
// `props`, so the markup ships exactly once. `CardStack.svelte` renders it with
// `{@render children?.()}` for the SSR-seeded entry, inside the same keyed
// `{#each}` every other entry goes through.
//
// The one thing that could not come with it is the declared width. It used to
// be read out of the rendered string during component init, so the correct
// `--max-width` was in the very first paint; slot content is DOM, not a string
// available at init. The width is therefore passed down explicitly by the two
// routes that already know it (`card.width` / `lens.width` — the same values
// that become `data-width` on the fragment).
interface Props {
  activeUid?: string;
  initialWidth?: string;
}
const { activeUid, initialWidth } = Astro.props;
import CardStack from './CardStack.svelte';
---

{/* `--max-width` is restated on the shell because the pre-paint skeleton hangs
    off it, OUTSIDE the island — so it cannot inherit the value the island
    renders inline on `#card-stack`, and would measure a 960px lens's fan
    against the 680px default. Same source, same moment, one line. */}
<div class="stack-shell" style={initialWidth ? `--max-width: ${initialWidth};` : undefined}>
  <CardStack client:load {activeUid} {initialWidth}>
    <slot />
  </CardStack>
  {/* The pre-paint fan skeleton's one effect (issue #122).

      Base.astro's head script built the markup — it knows the entry counts and
      the build-time placement table — but nothing it needs exists yet in
      <head>, and a script that waited (DOMContentLoaded, an observer) would
      race the very first paint it exists to beat. This runs inline immediately
      after the island, which is still before paint.

      OUTSIDE the island, and that is not a preference — it is MEASURED. The
      skeleton was first appended as a trailing child of `#card-stack`, on the
      reasoning that hydration walks its children in order and never looks past
      the last block. It does look: with the skeleton there, 0 of 51 tagged SSR
      nodes survived hydration and the active card's element reference was
      replaced — #120's failure exactly, which on a lens page means the filter
      panel and the browse results never come alive. Without it, 51 of 51. So
      `.stack-shell` exists to be a positioning box the island does not own,
      and the layer hangs off that instead.

      After the island, never before: an ahead spine tucks 4px over the active
      card's edge and belongs on top of it, and being last is the whole of the
      painting order (see the .stack-skeleton rules in global.css). */}
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var h = window.__pdyxsStackSkeleton;
      var el = h && document.currentScript.parentElement;
      if (el) el.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', h);
    })();
  </script>
</div>
